Lau reached Camp II on 16 September and stayed overnight before beginning his descent the following morning, according to Lakpa Sherpa, founder of 8K Expeditions. During the descent, he stopped to rest and lost his pulse within a minute, Mr Lakpa told The Straits Times.

A doctor and other climbers attended to Lau but were unable to save him, according to the Himalayan Times .

Lau had arrived in Samagaun on 7 September as part of an expedition attempting to climb the 8,163m mountain during Nepal’s autumn climbing season, the Rising Nepal reported .

